GitLab MCP Server – OAuth, ALB Workaround and AI Client Integration

1. Overview
This document describes the workaround required to enable the GitLab MCP Server integration with external AI clients such as:

Claude Desktop
Claude Code
GitHub Copilot in VS Code
Potentially other MCP-compatible AI clients
The workaround was suggested by GitLab Support because the MCP/OAuth discovery endpoints required by external AI clients were not being correctly routed when GitLab was hosted under the /gitlab subpath behind the Application Load Balancer (ALB).

The affected OAuth discovery endpoints are:

/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource

Because GitLab is hosted under:

/gitlab

the requests need to be rewritten to the corresponding /gitlab/.well-known/... paths.

2. GitLab Support Workaround
GitLab Support suggested adding NGINX rewrite rules to the GitLab Rails configuration.

The workaround consists of two changes:

Update the Production GitLab Rails gitlab.rb configuration.
Add the required /.well-known paths to the GitLab ALB listener rules.

3. Step 1 – Update gitlab.rb
Update the gitlab.rb configuration on the Production GitLab Rails servers.

Add the following configuration:

# Workaround for GitLab Support ticket #728398
nginx['custom_gitlab_server_config'] = <<~NGINX
rewrite ^(/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server)$ /gitlab$1 last;
rewrite ^(/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource)$ /gitlab$1 last;
NGINX

Purpose of the Rewrite Rules
The rewrite rules ensure that requests to:

/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server

are internally redirected to:

/gitlab/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server

Similarly:

/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource

is redirected to:

/gitlab/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource

This is required because the GitLab instance is hosted under the /gitlab subpath.

4. Apply the Configuration on GitLab Rails Servers
After updating gitlab.rb, apply the configuration on both Production GitLab Rails servers.

Run:

gitlab-ctl reconfigure

The command must be executed on both Rails servers to ensure the configuration is applied consistently.

5. Step 2 – Update ALB Listener Rules
The GitLab Application Load Balancer (ALB) listener rules must also be updated.

Add the following paths:

/.well-known
/.well-known/*

These listener rules allow the OAuth/MCP discovery requests to reach the GitLab infrastructure correctly.

Required ALB Paths
Path	Purpose
/.well-known	Handles the .well-known discovery path
/.well-known/*	Handles the OAuth discovery endpoints below .well-known

The relevant OAuth endpoints are:

/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource

6. MCP Testing with AI Clients
After the Rails NGINX configuration and ALB listener rules are updated, the GitLab MCP Server can be tested with AI clients.

The following use cases have been tested/documented:

Claude Desktop
GitHub Copilot in VS Code

7. Use Case 1 – Connect Claude Desktop with GitLab MCP Server
Prerequisites
Before configuring Claude Desktop, ensure that:

Node.js version 20 or later is installed.
Node.js is available globally in the PATH environment variable.
node can be found using:
which -a node

8. Configure GitLab MCP Server in Claude Desktop
Open Claude Desktop.

Edit the Claude Desktop configuration using either of the following methods.

Option 1 – Claude Desktop Settings
Navigate to:

Settings > Developer > Edit Config

Option 2 – macOS Configuration File
On macOS, open:

~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json

9. Add the GitLab MCP Server Configuration
Add the following configuration:

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "GitLab": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y",
        "mcp-remote",
        "https://dot-portal.de.pri.o2.com/gitlab/api/v4/mcp"
      ]
    }
  }
}

If npx is installed locally instead of globally, provide the full path to npx in the command parameter.

For example, instead of:

"command": "npx"

use the full path to the executable where required.

10. Save and Restart Claude Desktop
After adding the configuration:

Save the configuration file.
Restart Claude Desktop.
On the first connection, Claude Desktop should open a browser window for OAuth authentication.
Review the authorization request.
Approve the request.

11. Verify the Claude MCP Connection
After authentication:

Navigate to:

Settings > Developer

Verify that the new GitLab MCP configuration is present.

Then navigate to:

Settings > Connectors

and inspect the connected GitLab MCP server.

Once connected, start a new chat and ask questions based on the available MCP tools.

