20. Use Case 2 – Connect GitHub Copilot in VS Code
GitHub Copilot in VS Code uses HTTP transport for a direct connection to the GitLab MCP server.

This means no additional mcp-remote dependency is required for the direct HTTP connection.

21. Configure GitLab MCP Server in GitHub Copilot
Open Visual Studio Code.

Open the Command Palette.

macOS
Press:

Command + Shift + P

Windows/Linux
Press:

Control + Shift + P

Search for:

MCP: Add Server

and press Enter.

22. Select HTTP Server Type
For the server type, select:

HTTP

For the server URL, enter:

https://dot-portal.de.pri.o2.com/gitlab/api/v4/mcp

23. Save the MCP Configuration
Save the configuration either:

Globally/user configuration
Workspace configuration in vscode/mcp.json
The OAuth authorization page should then appear.

24. OAuth Authorization
In the browser:

Review the authorization request.
Approve the authorization request.
Return to VS Code.
Once authorized, GitHub Copilot can communicate with the GitLab MCP server.

25. Check MCP Server Status in VS Code
If the OAuth page does not appear, open the VS Code Command Palette and search for:

MCP: Show MCP Dashboard

Use the MCP Dashboard to:

Check the MCP server status.
Verify whether the server is connected.
Restart the MCP server if required.
