38. Final Summary
The GitLab MCP integration required an additional routing workaround because the GitLab instance is hosted under the /gitlab subpath behind an AWS ALB.

The implementation requires both:

NGINX rewrite rules on the GitLab Rails servers, and
ALB listener rules for /.well-known and /.well-known/*.
Once these changes are applied, external AI clients can successfully complete OAuth discovery and authenticate against the GitLab MCP server.

The integration was successfully verified with Claude Desktop, including:

OAuth authentication
MCP server connection
get_mcp_server_version
GitLab issue lookup
GitLab issue creation

GitHub Copilot in VS Code can connect directly using HTTP transport, with the recommendation to use the user/global MCP configuration if workspace-level configuration causes connection problems.

This setup provides AI clients with authenticated access to GitLab functionality through the MCP server while maintaining OAuth authorization and approval controls for operations that modify GitLab resources.

